 "md": [
  "# FlexGen blade — blade\n\n* Material: **Steel 4130**, boundary **fixed-guided**\n* L = 80.0 mm, b = 30.0 mm, t = 2.00 → 2.00 mm, mass 37.7 g\n* Rate at ride: **102.68 N/mm** at the tip (axial preload 0 N); strain energy at full travel 462 N·mm\n* Computed axial buckling load: **6004 N** (discrete tangent-stiffness eigenvalue, not a chart)\n* Parasitic stiffness ratio (stiff/compliant plane): 225\n\n## Lint\n* ✅ `A` — a\n* ⚠️ `B` — b|c\n* ⛔ `C` — c\n\n_Pre-validation output. Validate the blade in ANSYS (non-linear, large deflection) and fatigue-test a coupon with the production edge finish before cutting metal._\n",
  "# FlexGen blade — blade\n\n* Material: **Steel 4130**, boundary **fixed-guided**\n* L = 80.0 mm, b = 30.0 mm, t = 2.00 → 2.00 mm, mass 37.7 g\n* Rate at ride: **102.68 N/mm** at the tip (axial preload 0 N); strain energy at full travel 462 N·mm\n* Computed axial buckling load: **6004 N** (discrete tangent-stiffness eigenvalue, not a chart)\n* Parasitic stiffness ratio (stiff/compliant plane): 225\n\n## Lint\n\n## Coilover downsizing\n* Flexure supplies 33 % of the 30.0 N/mm wheel-rate target.\n* Residual physical spring: **20.0 N/mm** at the spring.\n\n_Pre-validation output. Validate the blade in ANSYS (non-linear, large deflection) and fatigue-test a coupon with the production edge finish before cutting metal._\n",
  "# FlexGen blade — blade\n\n* Material: **Steel 4130**, boundary **fixed-guided**\n* L = 80.0 mm, b = 30.0 mm, t = 2.00 → 2.00 mm, mass 37.7 g\n* Rate at ride: **102.68 N/mm** at the tip (axial preload 0 N); strain energy at full travel 462 N·mm\n* Computed axial buckling load: **6004 N** (discrete tangent-stiffness eigenvalue, not a chart)\n* Parasitic stiffness ratio (stiff/compliant plane): 225\n\n## Lint\n* ✅ `A` — a\n\n## Coilover downsizing\n* Flexure supplies 200 % of the 5.0 N/mm wheel-rate target.\n* ⛔ The blades ALONE exceed the wheel-rate target — the corner is over-sprung with no coilover fitted. Soften the blade.\n\n_Pre-validation output. Validate the blade in ANSYS (non-linear, large deflection) and fatigue-test a coupon with the production edge finish before cutting metal._\n"
